{"campaign_id": "rq2_multimodel_held_out", "citations": [{"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2023A", "artifact_type": "test_log", "relevance_note": "Indicates the existence of confidence-score logging mechanisms in release v23, highlighting that data gaps (missing logs for this specific episode) represent a critical failure in traceability and monitoring capabilities."}, {"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2027A", "artifact_type": "test_log", "relevance_note": "Indicates the existence of confidence-score logging mechanisms in release v27, providing context on system capabilities versus the specific failure instance described."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.10-b-regulatory-crossrefs", "artifact_type": "regulatory_citation", "relevance_note": "Cites ISO 13485 Clause 7.5.9.1 (Traceability) and part 821, which requires manufacturers to document procedures for traceability; the loss of device-side logs during a critical event represents a potential non-compliance with these traceability requirements."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.45-labeling", "artifact_type": "regulatory_citation", "relevance_note": "Cites 21 CFR \u00a7 820.45 regarding labeling and packaging controls including UDI; while less direct, the lack of retained logs impacts the ability to uniquely identify device instances involved in adverse events for reporting under part 830 referenced in qmsr-820.10-b-regulatory-crossrefs."}, {"artifact_id": "mdr-art83-pms-system", "artifact_type": "regulatory_citation", "relevance_note": "Cites EU MDR Article 83 regarding the Post-market surveillance system, which must actively and systematically gather relevant data on safety; the missing logs prevent this systematic gathering for a specific high-risk event."}], "contradiction_status": [], "escalated": false, "evidence_gaps": [], "evidence_requests": 0, "final_report": {"claim_support": [{"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2023A", "claim": "The incident narrative describes a realized serious harm (patient lost consciousnes